{title: Three Times a Day}
{subtitle: Daniel 6:1–29}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
They searched his life for something wrong, but not a fault was there to see
So they went to King Darius with a ban and a decree
[Cm7]For thirty days, no prayer to any god or man but [Gm]you
[D7]And the law of Medes and Persians [Cm7]says that no one can un[Gm]do
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When Daniel learned the ban [Cm7]was signed, he went home and [Gm]climbed the stair
To the upper room with windows [Cm7]open toward Jerusalem in [Gm]prayer
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Three times a day he got down on his [Cm7]knees
Giving thanks to his [Gm]God
Just as he had always [Cm7]done
Three times a [Ebmaj7]day, three [D7]times [Gm]a day
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
They threw him in the lions' den, a [Cm7]stone was laid upon the door [Gm][Cm7]
[Gm]The king sealed it with his signet [Cm7]ring, and he could do no [Gm]more [Cm7]
[Gm]He went back to his palace [Cm7]and he fasted through the [Gm]night [Cm7]
[Gm]And sleep fled from him, till [Cm7]he ran to the den at first [Gm]light [Cm7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Gm]Daniel, servant of [Cm7]the living God, the king cried [Gm]out in fear [Cm7]
[Gm]Has the God you serve conti[Cm7]nually been able to save you [Gm]here [Cm7]
[Gm]And Daniel called, O [Cm7]king, live forever, [Gm]no harm has come to me [Cm7]
[Gm]They lifted him out of the [Cm7]den, and not a wound [Gm]was there to see [Cm7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
My God sent his angel and shut the mouths of [Gm]the lions
[Cm7]He rescues and he saves
He is [D7]the living God, enduring forever
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Three [Gm]times a day he got down on his [Cm7]knees
Giving thanks to his [Gm]God
Just as he had always [Cm7]done
Three times a [Ebmaj7]day, three [D7]times [Gm]a day
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Cm7]Just as he had al[Gm]ways [Cm7]done
{end_of_verse}

